{
    "background_story": "Cullen was a skilled midwife who had dedicated his life to helping women bring new life into the world. He had delivered countless babies, but one particular birth stood out in his mind. It was a difficult delivery, and the mother, a young woman named Sarah, had suffered a severe hemorrhage after giving birth. Cullen's quick thinking and expertise saved her life, but not before she had lost a significant amount of blood. As he tended to her wounds, Cullen couldn't help but think about the afterbirth, the placenta that had nourished the baby for nine months. He realized that just as the placenta had given life to the child, his own actions had given Sarah a second chance at life. From that day on, Cullen felt a deeper sense of purpose in his work, knowing that he was not just delivering babies, but also giving mothers a chance to thrive after birth.",
